{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791642020,"nonce":"HtNJuY3mAvmcD1ixEOhVeYF3qH8=","title":"cn sidebar and tree view rebuild on every toggle and selection","message":"- sidebar: the rail was a Stateful with deps on the collapse flag and the selected item, so collapsing and every click rebuilt every item; each item chose icon-only or icon-and-label at build, and the toggle was a nested Stateful\u003cButtonState\u003e for its chevron.\n- tree view: one Stateful over the whole tree with deps on every node's expand state and the selection; a node's children were shut with a build-time `h(0)`.\n\nFix: both are built once.\n\n- sidebar: an item keeps its icon and shows its label through `visible` over the expanded state, so the rail's width changes in place and its keyed size animation follows; titles show through `when`; `cn-sidebar-item--active` is class_when and the icon colour a computed over the selection (falling back to the builder's active item before anything is selected); the toggle's chevron turns by a bound rotation.\n- tree view: a node's children collapse with `collapsed_when` over its expand state; the chevron turns 90 degrees; selection is class_when `cn-tree-node--selected` with the fill and label colour computeds. The dead container FSM and signal-id collection are removed.\n\nTests: `blinc_cn/tests/sidebar_in_place.rs` (collapsing narrows the rail in place; the width animates and settles; choosing an item moves the active mark) and `blinc_cn/tests/tree_in_place.rs` (clicking opens and selects in place; the height animates). All fail against the old components.","files":null}]}